  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct hydromorphone absolute oral bioavailability record is present in the visible L1 set.",
    "No affirmative F <20% record for a close opioid analogue is present; the lowest relevant positive is meptazinol at 27.9%.",
    "Several opioid records were obtained in cirrhosis patients, a condition that can alter first-pass metabolism; the direction remains positive but exact quantitative transfer to healthy hydromorphone is uncertain.",
    "No dose-, formulation-, or prandial-state-matched hydromorphone data are available."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "All visible L1 records with relevant opioid scaffolds report F above 20% (meptazinol 27.9%, pentazocine 68–70%, codeine 80.5%, pethidine 80%, naloxegol 90%); the query is a morphinan opioid structurally related to these contexts, and no affirmative evidence supports F <20%. Therefore predict high with moderate confidence."
}

